//! The `clear` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets whether an
//! element must be moved below (cleared)
//! [floating](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/float) elements
//! that precede it. The `clear` property applies to floating and non-floating elements.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: inline-start | inline-end | block-start | block-end | left | right | top | bottom |
//! both-inline | both-block | both | none
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-page-floats-3/#propdef-clear
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/clear
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

